# Code Language Conventions

This governs the language used in code itself: identifiers, and the strings the code produces at runtime, error messages above all.

---

## Language of the code

- Every identifier is written in `{{.Language.Code}}`.
- Every string the code throws, returns as an error or logs is written in `{{.Language.Code}}`, even when the class or function name already is.
{{if .Language.UI}}
## Language of the interface

- The text a user reads on screen is written in `{{.Language.UI}}`.
- An error shown to the user is made in two steps: the code returns an error in `{{.Language.Code}}`, and the UI layer maps it to `{{.Language.UI}}` copy. The `{{.Language.UI}}` text never lives inside the thrown error.
{{end}}
---

## Non-goals

- Says nothing about comments in conversation, commit messages or any file outside the code.
